b $4000 Display File
D $4000 There is no loading screen. The tape loads through the ROM loader,
. and leaves the display file mostly clear. The picture below is the opening
. screen as drawn by the BASIC program (captured after autorun reaches ROM
. PAUSE at #N($1F3D,$04,$04)).
D $4000 #PUSHS #OPENINGPOKES
. #UDGTABLE
. { =h Opening screen (as drawn by the BASIC program). }
. { #SCR$02(opening) }
. UDGTABLE#
. #POPS
@ $4000 label=DisplayFile
  $4000,$1800,$20 Pixels.
  $5800,$0300,$20 Attributes.

i $5B00
i $5C00

b $5CCB BASIC Program
@ $5CCB label=BasicProgram
D $5CCB #HTML(Velnor's Lair by Derek Brewster, published by Neptune Computing
. in 1983. It is the first of his two "Myths and Legends of Caraland"
. games; <a href="https://spectrumcomputing.co.uk/entry/7157"
. rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Spectrum Computing</a> also notes
. the Quicksilva reissue and the sequel, Kentilla.)
N $5CCB #HTML(The whole game is a ROM-loaded BASIC program. The tape header
. names it "VELNOR", sets autorun at line 4860, and gives a program length of
. #N($93D2,$04,$04) and a data length of #N($A112,$04,$04). There is no
. custom tape loader.)
N $5CCB #HTML(Line 4860 is <code>POKE D,F: GO TO A</code> with the saved
. variables <code>D=23728</code> (#SKOOLKID$5CB0(NMIADD)), <code>F=4</code>
. and <code>A=1</code>, so it writes #N($04) to NMIADD and starts at line 5.
. Line 4870 (<code>PRINT USR TU</code>) is not the autorun path.)
N $5CCB #HTML(The command loop at line 113 reads
. <code>WHAT WILL YOU DO NOW ?</code>. Movement updates BASIC variable
. <code>Z</code> (the location's own line number: north/south by #N($5F),
. east/west by #N($05)) and line 530 <code>GO SUB Z</code> prints the room.
. See the recovered listing on the #LINK(Basic)(BASIC listing) page.)
N $5CCB #HTML(Line 6035 POKEs a #N($10)-byte routine at #R$FF58 that writes
. attribute #N($38) across the screen; line 6330 calls it with
. <code>RANDOMIZE USR 65368</code>. That code is not on the tape and is not
. present in this snapshot.)
  $5CCB,$13 Line 5: INK 7: LET V=A: GO SUB VAL "6E3".
  $5CDE,$15 Line 10: LET Z=VAL "7030": LET Z1=Z.
  $5CF3,$0C Line 20: GO SUB VAL "3E3".
  $5CFF,$12 Line 80: IF HP<=O THEN GO TO VAL "103".
  $5D11,$27 Line 81: IF X=VAL "13" AND M(VAL "13")=NM AND NM=O THEN GO TO VAL
. "6080".
  $5D38,$0C Line 85: INK O: PRINT : GO SUB Z.
  $5D44,$0E Line 90: PRINT : GO SUB VAL "555".
  $5D52,$0A Line 95: LET Z1=Z.
  $5D5C,$19 Line 100: IF O(VAL "14")>O THEN GO SUB VAL "4800".
  $5D75,$0D Line 101: LET HP=HP-B.
  $5D82,$47 Line 103: IF BORD AND A+HP/IHP*SE<=BORD THEN LET BORD=BORD-A: BEEP
. TU/A,BORD: BORDER BORD: IF BORD THEN GO TO VAL "103".
  $5DC9,$15 Line 105: IF BORD=O THEN GO TO VAL "6100".
  $5DDE,$29 Line 106: INK O: IF O(F)=A THEN GO SUB VAL "4500": LET Z1=Z: GO SUB
. Z: GO SUB VAL "555".
